@node Health
@chapter Health
@cindex health
@findex gascity-health
@kindex j h

@kbd{j h} (or @kbd{M-x gascity-health}) opens
@file{*gascity-health:@: CITY*} in @code{gascity-health-mode}: the
city's plumbing, one section per @command{gc} read so that one failure
never blanks the others.

@example
Health  bright-lights                                         ▲ watch
Supervisor
  pid 22262 · supervisor · ▲ degraded (no_agents_running) · not suspended
Versions
  gc 1.4.2 · bd 1.3.0 · dolt 2.3.5 · store NativeDoltStore
Store  ◐
  ~/bright-lights/.beads/dolt        109 MB   threshold 1 MB/row
  ◐ store health: runtime status probe incomplete
  ● dolt :41586 · pid 23571 · 120 ms · 2 databases
  size (this session)  ▁▁▂▂▃
Rig stores  1
  ● hello-world    ~/hello-world                              dolt ok
Doctor  88 passed · 5 warned · 0 failed · ran 4m ago   ! run  F run --fix
  ▲ formula-requirements         blocking  36 formula requirement warning(s)
  ▸ 88 checks ok
@end example

@shot{health-dark, Health of emacs-city (ef-elea-dark)}

@section What it shows

@table @asis
@item The top line
The city (with @samp{@@host} for a remote one) and an overall verdict:
@samp{■ attention} when the controller is down, the city is unusable,
the Dolt server is not running, a doctor check failed or a rig store
cannot be read; @samp{▲ watch} when the city is degraded, the store is
over its size threshold, @command{gc} reports partial errors, or
doctor warned; else @samp{● ok}.  While the host is unreachable it
reads @samp{○ offline @@host}.
@item Supervisor
From @code{gc status}: the controller's pid and mode, health
(@samp{health ok}, @samp{▲ degraded (@var{signals})} or @samp{■
unusable}) and whether the city is suspended.
@item Versions
@code{gc version}, and the beads store kind from @code{gc status}.  The
@command{bd} and @command{dolt} versions appear once doctor has run:
its report is the only place @command{gc} exposes them.
@item Store
From @code{gc status}: the store's path, size, rows-per-megabyte ratio
and threshold, a @samp{▲} line when the store is over it and a
@samp{◐} line per partial error.  From @code{gc dolt health}: the Dolt
server's port, pid, latency and database count, with @samp{▲} lines for
orphan databases, zombie processes or stale backups; @key{RET} on the
server line opens the Dolt list.  Then @samp{size (this session)}, a
@samp{▁▂▃} sparkline of the store sizes sampled this session (every
status read the cockpit or this view got; the tooltip gives the range).
@item Rig stores
One @code{gc rig status @var{name}} per rig: @samp{● dolt ok} when the
rig's beads are initialized and its Dolt database exists, @samp{▲} with
the reason otherwise, @samp{○ suspended}, or @samp{■} with the error for
a rig whose read failed.  @key{SPC} shows the rig's prefix, branch and
agents; @key{RET} opens its dashboard; @kbd{l} its git log.
@item Doctor
The last @command{gc doctor} report of the session: counts and how long
ago it ran.  Failed checks, then warnings, get a row each ---
@samp{■ @var{name}  @var{severity}  @var{message}} --- and @key{SPC}
opens a check's fix hint and details.  Passing checks fold into
@samp{▸ N checks ok}.
@end table

@section Keys

@table @kbd
@item !
@kindex ! @r{(health)}
@findex gascity-health-doctor
Run @command{gc doctor} in the background.  It is never run on open or
on @kbd{g} --- it takes tens of seconds --- so the section reads
@samp{not run} until you ask.  While it runs the header reads
@samp{running@dots{}} and the rest of the view stays usable; the report
is cached for the session, so reopening the view shows it with its age.
Doctor has its own deadline, @code{gascity-health-doctor-timeout}.
@item F
@kindex F @r{(health)}
@findex gascity-health-doctor-fix
Run @command{gc doctor --fix} after a confirmation, in the background,
the same way.
@item g
@kindex g @r{(health)}
@findex gascity-health-refresh
Re-read every section but Doctor.
@item @key{RET}
@kindex RET @r{(health)}
@findex gascity-health-activate
On a rig, open its dashboard; on the Store header or Dolt line, the Dolt
list; on the Rig stores header, the rig list; on the Doctor header, run
doctor.
@end table

