@node The Mode-Line Lighter
@chapter The Mode-Line Lighter
@cindex mode-line lighter
@cindex lighter
@findex gascity-mode-line-mode

@code{gascity-mode-line-mode} is a global minor mode, off by default,
that shows what needs you in every open city in every mode line:

@example
 GC[bl ▲1 · ec ■1▲2]
@end example

@shot{lighter-dark, The lighter in the mode line (ef-elea-dark)}

@noindent
One segment per open cockpit: the city's initials (@samp{emacs-city}
@result{} @samp{ec}; a remote one adds @samp{@@host}), then its Needs
you totals --- @samp{■} attention and @samp{▲} watch --- or @samp{●}
when it needs nothing.  @kbd{mouse-1} on a segment shows that city's
cockpit; the tooltip spells the counts out.  Killing a cockpit drops its
segment.

The counts are the ones each cockpit publishes when it renders
(@pxref{The Cockpit}).  The lighter never runs @command{gc} and never
touches a remote host: its mode-line construct is a string rebuilt only
when a count changes, so redisplay does no work at all.

@lisp
(gascity-mode-line-mode 1)
@end lisp

@noindent
With live refresh (@pxref{Live Refresh}) the cockpit re-renders when an
event arrives, so the lighter follows the city's event stream.

